 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It depends on how many languages you handle carefully. Dutch and Norwegian share a million word vocabulary, much more than English does for either. Sound similarities matter a lot. If you recognize a few words automatically, you think you' being smart, and that helps a lot. Dutch also has simple vowel and consonant pronunciation, much simpler than many Englishers fear. Norwegian uses different letters where Dutch keeps them, so a small letter of the alphabet is useful. On the whole, I' say Dutch. If you end up with a native speaker as your partner, you can switch to them for words you see.",
